For each gene, we will randomly choose a value from the search space. However, if the gene corresponds to a parameter that has been shown to perform well in previous runs (e.g., activation type, learning rate), we will give it a higher probability of selecting one of the top-performing values. This way, we can leverage the knowledge from the best known architecture while still exploring other parts of the search space.

